{"case_id":"C038","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":90,"change_types":["configuration-dependent behavior","input-processing path modification"],"affected_functions":["spng_set_crc_action","read_and_check_crc","read_header","get_ancillary_data_first_idat","validate_past_idat"],"reason":"The commit adds functional handling for SPNG_CRC_DISCARD on ancillary CRC mismatches, but the harness fixes both CRC policies to SPNG_CRC_USE. Consequently, fuzz input cannot reach the new discard behavior. The existing decode path remains suitable for the stored-chunk bitmask refactor and cache-discard changes, but its fixed CRC configuration is inadequate for the newly implemented CRC-policy path.","evidence":["H0 always calls spng_set_crc_action(ctx, SPNG_CRC_USE, SPNG_CRC_USE).","read_and_check_crc() now returns SPNG_CRC_DISCARD when an ancillary CRC mismatches and crc_action_ancillary is SPNG_CRC_DISCARD.","read_header() now accepts an int *discard parameter and specially handles SPNG_CRC_DISCARD.","The remaining stored_* to ctx->stored bitmask changes preserve existing APIs and are reached by the harness through spng_decoded_image_size() and spng_decode_image()."],"recommended_action":"Update the harness to exercise multiple CRC policies, including SPNG_CRC_DISCARD for ancillary chunks, while retaining the current SPNG_CRC_USE decode configuration."}
